-- title:
--   RFC 8439, §2.5.2 and A.3 — poly1305_mac on the example and test vectors #1–#11
-- statement:
--   `poly1305Mac` (RFC 8439 §2.5.1, in the bundle `Poly1305Boringssl_Rfc8439`) gives the printed tag on twelve inputs: the example of §2.5.2 (the 34-byte message “Cryptographic Forum Research Group”) and the eleven test vectors of Appendix A.3. Each conjunct is `poly1305Mac msg key = tag` with the message, the 32-byte key and the 16-byte tag as printed, byte for byte. For A.3 #1–#4 the key is the printed “One-time Poly1305 Key”; for #5–#11, which print “R” and “S” separately, it is the 16 bytes of R followed by the 16 bytes of S. The messages have 34, 64, 375, 375, 127, 16, 16, 48, 48, 16, 64 and 48 bytes.
--
--   RFC 8439, §2.5.2, p. 18: “Tag: a8:06:1d:c1:30:51:36:c6:c2:2b:8b:af:0c:01:27:a9”, for the key and message printed above it; Appendix A.3, pp. 36–41: “Test Vector #1” to “Test Vector #11”, each a key (or R and S), a text and a tag.
-- source:
